message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Open Road Risk: an open-data pipeline for exposure-adjusted collision risk on the GB road network"
abstract: >-
  Open Road Risk is a staged open-data pipeline for estimating exposure-adjusted
  collision risk on the GB road network. It combines DfT STATS19 collision records,
  DfT AADF traffic counts, OS Open Roads geometry, National Highways WebTRIS sensor
  data, OpenStreetMap attributes, population, deprivation, and rural-urban context
  to produce link-level risk scores for OS Open Roads links across Great Britain,
  excluding Northern Ireland (2015–2024).
type: software
